Upstream: t3code
--------------------

Botki is a fork of t3code (https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code), the agent harness
control surface developed by T3 Tools Inc. The server, the v2 orchestrator and its
event-sourced projections, the provider adapters, the checkpointing layer, and the web
and desktop clients are upstream's work, used here under the MIT License reproduced in
full in the LICENSE file alongside this notice.

    Copyright (c) 2026 T3 Tools Inc.
    Licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

Botki removes large parts of upstream — account auth, hosted relay and guest sharing,
forge and pull-request integrations, the code editor, and outbound telemetry — and adds
the nightly agent loop around what remains. Any defect in what is left is ours, not
upstream's. Upstream is not responsible for, and does not endorse, this fork.

Design ideas referenced
-----------------------

Botki's product direction — a local-first host that runs coding agents on a schedule
against dedicated per-agent workspaces, keeps a task queue, and reports back without a
human in the loop — was informed by OpenBot (https://github.com/nightly-labs/openbot),
specifically releases up to and including v0.1.11, which were distributed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

    Copyright (c) The OpenBot authors
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

What Botki takes from OpenBot is ideas about how a night of agent work should be
organized: what a bot is, what a slice is, and where a hand-off belongs. No OpenBot
source code, binary, or asset is distributed with Botki, and none is derived from it.

This attribution is bounded to OpenBot <= 0.1.11 deliberately. Later OpenBot releases are
distributed under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0, which is not compatible with
the MIT-licensed distribution of this repository; the ideas referenced here predate that
change and are attributed under the terms that applied to them.


Third-party notices
-------------------

Notices for npm and other third-party dependencies that ship in a build are generated
per client rather than listed here, so the text always matches what actually shipped:

- Web, desktop and the bundled server: `third-party-licenses.json`, generated beside
  `index.html` at build time and shown in Settings.
- Mobile: a generated module, built before each bundle.
- License templates come from the pinned SPDX License List, committed under
  `third-party-licenses/spdx/`.

Manually maintained exceptions (adapted icons, fonts, vendored native code, and other
assets that did not come from an npm package) are configured in
`third-party-licenses.config.json`, and their license text lives beside the code it
covers. See docs/internals/open-source-licenses.md.

The directories under `.repos/` are read-only vendored references kept for pattern
study. They are not compiled into or distributed with Botki; each carries its own
LICENSE and NOTICE.
